Mech footfalls
--------------
Heavy ground impacts and separate pneumatic strokes generated with ElevenLabs
Sound Effects v2 (eleven_text_to_sound_v2), October 2026. Edited as individual
one-shots for Starsector Marines; layered at runtime by per-foot gait events.
Prompts, original takes, generation receipts and offline mix recipe are retained
in asset-pipeline/src/tool/resources/audio/mech-footsteps/ and tools/.

Generated audio (ElevenLabs)
----------------------------
Every voice in the mod was generated with ElevenLabs on a paid Creator plan,
2026, for Starsector Marines, as were the generated sound effects and the
Jangala arrival score. Voices are original Voice Design characters or
ElevenLabs library voices; no game or real person's recording was uploaded or
cloned. All dialogue was written for this mod. Beyond the entries named above,
this covers:
  - Company officer responses (Company Officer B - British Matriarch)
  - Colony Breach speech and sound effects
  - Jangala arrival: hails, Castle's lines, background effects and the score
  - The battle music's quiet bed: the arrival score's strings take
  - Sabine and the Shepherd story voices
  - The Rook rifle shot
Prompts, voice ids, source takes and generation receipts are retained beside
each clip under asset-pipeline/src/tool/resources/audio/ and art-source/.

Original synthesized audio
--------------------------
The Jangala yard ambience, the tender sounds, and the arrival's cabin bed, wind
and radio squelches are synthesized from scratch by the mod's own scripts
(ffmpeg and numpy), retained beside each clip.

Generated art
-------------
Most of the art under graphics/ and the Jangala arrival cinematic were made
for this mod with OpenAI image generation (Codex ImageGen and built-in
imagegen), refined and assembled by scripts and by hand, or rendered from the
mod's own Blender models. Prompts and masters are retained under art-source/.
A few battle sprites (the Venture and pirate Hound hulls and six fighter
craft) are up-scaled derivatives of Starsector's own sprites, used in a mod
for that game.

